    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d782">

                <pb facs="0819" n="807" xml:id="pg807"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.51 Frozen Credits/7788: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Caffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-09-23T18:00:00-03:00">September 23, 1942—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 8:35 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3786. My 1921, June 6, and Department’s instruction 3307, September 1.<anchor
                        n="64" xml:id="d782-f1"/> French Financial Attaché has again approached Bank
                    of Brazil requesting shipment of gold to Banco Central, Buenos Aires, for
                    account of Bank of International Settlements. In view of diplomatic nature of
                    case Director of Exchange has found it necessary to refer case to Minister of
                    Finance for decision.</p>
                <p>If Department believes that Bank of International Settlements is under Axis
                    control or acting on behalf of Axis interests and that shipment therefore should
                    not be permitted please telegraph so that I can inform Ministry of Foreign
                    Affairs.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
